&lt;p&gt;Demostrar con Lean4 y con Isabelle/HOL que
\[ s ∩ (s ∪ t) = s \]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Para ello, completar la siguiente teoría de Lean4:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code"&gt;&lt;pre class="code literal-block"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Mathlib.Tactic&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;α&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;α&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;example&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;∩&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;∪&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gr"&gt;sorry&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;y la siguiente teoría de Isabelle/HOL:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code"&gt;&lt;pre class="code literal-block"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;theory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Interseccion_con_su_union&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kp"&gt;imports&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Main&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;begin&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kn"&gt;lemma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"s ∩ (s ∪ t) = s"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gr"&gt;oops&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;wnd&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jaalonso.github.io/calculemus/posts/2021/05/25-interseccion_con_su_union/"&gt;Leer más…&lt;/a&gt; (quedan 4 minutos de lectura)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description><category>Conjuntos</category><category>Interseccióm</category><category>Isabelle</category><category>Lean4</category><guid>https://jaalonso.github.io/calculemus/posts/2021/05/25-interseccion_con_su_union/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 May 2021 04:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Demostraciones de "s ∩ t = t ∩ s"</title><link>https://jaalonso.github.io/calculemus/posts/2021/05/24-conmutatividad_de_la_interseccion/</link><dc:creator>José A. Alonso</dc:creator><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demostrar con Lean4 y con Isabelle/HOL que
\[ s ∩ t = t ∩ s \]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Para ello, completar la siguiente teoría de Lean4:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code"&gt;&lt;pre class="code literal-block"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;α&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;α&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;example&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;∩&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;∩&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gr"&gt;sorry&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;y la siguiente teoría de Isabelle/HOL:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code"&gt;&lt;pre class="code literal-block"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;theory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Conmutatividad_de_la_interseccion&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kp"&gt;imports&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Main&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;begin&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kn"&gt;lemma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"s ∩ t = t ∩ s"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="gr"&gt;oops&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

